  "body": "When the matrix specification says a type is a boolean, synapse accepts both `0`, `1`, `false` and `true` in the request, while only `false` and `true` are valid values.\r\n\r\nI've seen this behaviour in at least the typing API (https://github.com/matrix-org/sytest/pull/1088) and the register API (https://github.com/matrix-org/sytest/pull/1089)",
